// DeepSeek-V2-Lite FFN layer 0, 256-token prefill on 16 + 4 chiplets, variant all with mapping single_pass,
// as two passes of 128 rows, each a single pass over its rows: every weight chunk used for all 128 rows as it streams in (8 row tiles a GEMM, weights loaded into L1 once), the second pass copying each chunk from the L3 ring slot it landed in (16 slots hold all of a cluster's chunks); the down output reduced in 128-column slices; X multicast in 4 row blocks, the first gate|up chunk run per block (x_blocks); each store created one slice later (store_lag); a GEMM repeating the previous configuration runs as gemm_minimal (gemm_reuse); reshape + quantise in 4 row blocks (post_blocks) (fold, ChainGather, store) under the next slice. The root chip's clusters take the smaller column share (root_light); the first gate|up chunk two gate blocks wide (first_blocks); each cluster's first 4 weight chunks pushed one by one (weight_ring head, batch_head). The last gate|up chunk one GEMM per post block, its post-processing interleaved (split_last); the symmetric buffers not zeroed before the start, so the L1 plan lays them over X (sym_zero false); each chip's down projection split by output columns between its two clusters, so no partial is folded inside a chip and the gathers alternate between the clusters' xDMAs (dn_split cols); each cluster's first down slice one GEMM per post block, behind that block's A8 rows (split_first_dn); the columns split in 16-column units (col_unit) and cluster 0's share of the outputs moved so the busiest cluster has the fewest array steps (dn_balance); the root chip's clusters a block or two lighter than the busiest (root_cols); cluster 1's gathers run the ring the other way (chain_alt); the first down chunk's load ahead of the A8 copies (dn_load_early); dep-tag relays on the SIMD cores first (relay_on_simd); the first gather waits only for the copies into its own cluster, through the down GEMMs (first_gather_waits_copies false); each gather's dep-tag relays serve that gather alone (relay_per_gather); INT4 weights in the paired layout, read 64 bytes a pass (w4_paired). Between the passes: X of pass 2 multicast behind pass 1's gate|up loads, before its first gather; pass 2's first A8 copies after pass 1's last gather. Y over the X buffers in L3 (l3_overlay) and each chip's task-id maps holding only its own tasks (compact_id_maps), so the image fits the 8 MiB L3; 128-column slices (dn_cols) keep the root's two-pass buffers inside L1. ../../common/ffn_prefill_mc.py.
{
  num_chiplets: 16
  num_clusters: 2
  model: dsv2-lite-l0
  seed: 1
  tokens: 256
  rows: 128
  wbits: 4
  blocks: 3
  dn_cols: 128
  w_chunk_bytes: 98304
  w_buffers: 2
  x_buffers: 1
  weight_ring:
  {
    slots: 16
    batch: 4
    policy: 1
    head: 4
    batch_head: 1
  }
  weight_crest: false
  bcast: bcast_l1
  reduce: chain
  sync: edge
  static_l1: true
  compact_id_maps: true
  l3_overlay: true
  l1_capacity: 990000
  d2d_ddr: true
  mapping: single_pass
  deq_per_row: true
  x_blocks: 4
  store_lag: 1
  gemm_reuse: true
  post_blocks: 4
  root_light: true
  first_blocks: 2
  split_last: true
  sym_zero: false
  dn_split: cols
  split_first_dn: true
  col_unit: 16
  dn_balance: true
  root_cols: [320, 304]
  chain_alt: true
  dn_load_early: true
  relay_on_simd: true
  first_gather_waits_copies: false
  relay_per_gather: true
  w4_paired: true
}
